              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for to feed, then the Hindi for to be brought up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: किशोर",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "किशोर — kiśor — \"an adolescent; a teenager\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "किशोर उम्र में बच्चे बहुत जल्दी बदलते हैं। kiśor umr meṁ bacce bahut jaldī badalte haiṁ. In their teens, children change very quickly."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "किशोर (kiśor) is a tatsama, borrowed from Sanskrit kiśora, first \"a colt\" and then \"a youth, a lad\" (Monier-Williams). The feminine is kiśorī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
